# L0 / B007 — dependency-injection, development-workflow, docker, dotnet-testing.

C R196 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run code-review (or the code-reviewer agent) before the final verification and address real findings. | substantial work | none stated
C R197 OL WF-003 | MUST | Before declaring implementation complete run verify; a change is not complete while verification fails or is unreported. | implementation completion | none stated
C R198 OL RUN-012 | MUST | A performance-motivated change identifies the actual bottleneck or cost, preserves observable behavior, uses the simplest effective optimization, keeps or adds tests for the affected behavior, and benchmarks or profiles non-obvious or complex optimizations. | performance changes | none stated
C R199 OL GOV-002 | MUST | For a new application or substantial feature read SPECIFICATION.md (and any feature specification) before planning or implementing; read CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md when tunable values are involved. | new applications and substantial features | none stated
C R200 OL GOV-018 | MUST | Before implementing a questionable request name the concrete concern (duplication, poor cohesion, trigger or loading problems, context cost, conflict with architecture or policy, unnecessary complexity) and propose an alternative; this never authorizes silently rewriting or ignoring the user's requirement — the user decides. | questionable requests | none stated
C R201 OL PST-008 | MUST | Whenever a Domain or persistence change affects seeded entities (new required or renamed properties, changed relationships or enum/status values, new meaningful states, changed invariants), update the maintained development seeder in the same change so that recreating the Development database at this revision yields valid, representative data. | Domain and persistence changes | none stated
C R202 OL PST-010 | MUST | Treat migrations as source code: review each generated migration before committing it, paying particular attention to destructive schema changes, unexpected column recreation, data migrations, indexes, foreign keys and delete behavior. | EF Core migrations | none stated
C X16 EX PST-009,PST-010 | MUST | Schema changes are created as new EF Core migrations from the Infrastructure project with the Api project as startup project. | schema changes | none stated | The oracle requires a migration only for schema-affecting CUSTOM_SETTINGS changes (PST-009) and review of generated migrations (PST-010); it has no general rule that every schema change is made through a new migration with fixed projects. | A schema change applied through a hand-written SQL script or by editing an existing migration deviates from the workflow.
C X17 EX WF-009,GOV-017 | MUST | The development-workflow report summarizes what changed, the verify result block, unresolved Decision Requests and remaining known issues. | implementation work | none stated | WF-009 covers the verification state and GOV-017 the listing of unresolved Decision Requests in headless runs; a fixed summary of changes and remaining known issues for every implementation is an additional reporting duty. | A final message that reports only the verify block without the change summary and known issues does not follow the workflow.

